===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|other}}, from {{inh|en|ang|ōþer||other, second}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*ą̄þar}}, {{m|gmw-pro|*anþar}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*anþeraz||other, second}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*h₂énteros||other}}.

Cognate with {{cog|sco|uther}}, {{m|sco|ither||other}}, {{cog|ofs|oþer|ōther}}, {{gloss|"other"; > {{cog|frr|üđer}}, {{m|frr|ööder}}, {{m|frr|ouder}}}}, {{cog|osx|ōthar||other}}, {{cog|goh|ander||other}}, {{cog|non|annarr}}, {{m|non|ǫðrum|ǫðr-}}, {{m|non|aðru|aðr-|t=other, second}}, {{cog|got|𐌰𐌽𐌸𐌰𐍂||other}}, {{cog|prg|anters}}, {{m|prg|antars||other, second}}, {{cog|lt|antroks||other|pos=pronoun}}, {{cog|lv|otrs}}, {{m|lv|otrais||second}}, [[Macedonian]] ''[[втор]]'' (vtor, "second"), {{cog|sq|ndërroj||to change, switch, alternate}}, {{cog|sa|अन्तर|tr=ántara||different}}

{{m+|fr|autre}}, {{m+|es|otro}}, {{m+|pt|outro}}, etc., all from {{m+|la|alter}}, are [[false cognate|false cognate]]s.

