===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To regard, label{{,}} or treat as an "other", as not part of the same group; to view as different and [[alien]].
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Racetalk: racism hiding in plain sight|year=2005|author=Kristen A. Myers|passage="Rican" is code for its homonym, "redskin," through which they '''othered''' this non-Mexican ethnic group.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Challenging lesbian norms|year=2006|author=Angela Pattatucci Aragon|passage=That is, whilst Lesfest organisers are '''othering''' women who are not born female (thus producing a kind of lesbian-normativity), the Australian WOMAN Network is '''othering''' women who have not had surgical sex reassignment (thus producing a kind of "trans-normativity").}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2008|author=John F. Borland|publisher=University of Connecticut|title=The under-representation of Black females in NCAA Division I women's basketball head coaching positions|url=https://opencommons.uconn.edu/dissertations/AAI3325610/|passage={{...}} and Black males have not taken her seriously politically (gender); and the color of her skin has marginalized her (race and "'''othered'''" her when compared with White women, who have also worked to silence her political views.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Encyclopedia of Identity|year=2010|author=Ronald L. Jackson, I|passage=Others with admitted addictions are '''Othered''' and sadly, forever stigmatized.}}
